{{also|Monte|monté}}
==English==

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|es|monte||mountain}}: in the sense of the card game, referring to the stack of unplayed cards. {{doublet|en|mount}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/mɒnti/|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|ɒnti|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|uncountable|card games}} A game in which three or four [[card]]s are [[dealt]] [[face]]-[[up]] and [[player]]s [[bet]] on which of them will [[first]] be [[matched]] in [[suit]] by others dealt.
# {{lb|en|countable|Latin America}} A [[wood]] or [[forest]]; [[timberland]].

===Anagrams===
* {{anagrams|en|Monet|Moten|mento|mento-}}

